1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,800
On the franchise kiosk, Sam signs in with an identity owned by the franchise instead of a Harborline password.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,400
Entra recognizes the federated domain and redirects the browser to HarborPass for authentication.

3
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:23,000
HarborPass verifies Sam and multifactor, then returns a signed assertion so Entra can issue the application token.

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:31,700
The browser lands in the same Front Desk experience, with Harborline’s device and application rules still applied.

5
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:39,500
This separates responsibility cleanly: the franchise manages the credential, while Harborline controls access to its application.
